pe":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/commits/9d892f567117f2fe0043307a4be62e8d6236463c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:47:29Z","email":"shastry.sushruth@gmail.com","name":"Sushruth Sastry"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:47:29Z","email":"shastry.sushruth@gmail.com","name":"Sushruth Sastry"},"message":"fix(sandbox): mfe-b render returns unmount cleanup\n\nrender now accepts props and returns a cleanup fn that unmounts the\nnested mfe-a and removes its container, matching the MFE interface.","tree":{"sha":"ee8c2c77443ded88e630785e0e6d94343c55b7a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/git/trees/ee8c2c77443ded88e630785e0e6d94343c55b7a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/git/commits/9d892f567117f2fe0043307a4be62e8d6236463c","verification":{"payload":"tree ee8c2c77443ded88e630785e0e6d94343c55b7a4\nparent 762d274858a95c844806fde382aed24e0e9a16ce\nauthor Sushruth Sastry <shastry.sushruth@gmail.com> 1788907649 -0700\ncommitter Sushruth Sastry <shastry.sushruth@gmail.com> 1788907649 -0700\n\nfix(sandbox): mfe-b render returns unmount cleanup\n\nrender now accepts props and returns a cleanup fn that unmounts the\nnested mfe-a and removes its container, matching the MFE interface.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgihZXykC7fng3CqlgGfNFC1mDFV\nZZHK/+4dgh+F8J5O4AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHcPcyJ4NeWe2hbfUFmWOk+hyPPZeA2eQjCfUmfGddD0kOZtxMK/PEHFcHHJ3fYB8L\nvdSL08xGU1HoSzBABoYgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T22:47:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2114206?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sushruth","id":2114206,"login":"sushruth","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTQyMDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/usually-frustrated/fe/commit/9d892f567117f2fe0043307a4be62e8d6236463c","node_id":"C_kwDOQyVLeNoAKDlkODkyZjU2NzExN2YyZmUwMDQzMzA3YTRiZTYyZThkNjIzNjQ2M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/usually-frustrated/fe/commit/762d274858a95c844806fde382aed24e0e9a16ce","sha":"762d274858a95c844806fde382aed24e0e9a16ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/commits/762d274858a95c844806fde382aed24e0e9a16ce"}],"sha":"9d892f567117f2fe0043307a4be62e8d6236463c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/commits/9d892f567117f2fe0043307a4be62e8d6236463c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2114206?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sushruth","id":2114206,"login":"sushruth","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTQyMDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/commits/762d274858a95c844806fde382aed24e0e9a16ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:49:26Z","email":"2114206+sushruth@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sushruth Sastry"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:49:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(syntax-highlighter): add CSS line numbers via data-linenumbers (#36)\n\n* feat(syntax-highlighter): add CSS line numbers via data-linenumbers\n\nLine count is computed as a by-product of the existing tokenizer pass\nin highlightPre (no second traversal). The count is written as the\ndata-linenumbers attribute value; CSS ::before { content: attr(...) }\nrenders the number column with zero new DOM nodes injected into code.\n\nBlocks with data-linenumbers scroll horizontally rather than wrap, so\nline numbers stay aligned against long lines.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* refactor(syntax-highlighter): restore applySheet as named function\n\nWas inlined unnecessarily to hit a hard line limit. The limit is a\nguideline; 181 lines is fine.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* docs: soften source file line limit to a guideline (σ≈5 around 180)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* fix(syntax-highlighter): enforce no-wrap invariant with !important\n\nwhite-space, overflow-x, and min-width are correctness constraints for\nline number alignment, not style preferences. !important prevents\naccidental CSS overrides from silently breaking number sync.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* feat(syntax-highlighter): release 0.3.0 with line numbers; update docs\n\n- Bump version 0.2.3 → 0.3.0\n- Add CHANGELOG.md\n- Add data-linenumbers to file/source code blocks in docs fragments\n  (architecture, platform-eng, product-eng, tutorials); shell commands\n  and short concept snippets left unchanged\n\nTo publish: cd toolkit/syntax-highlighter && bun run publish\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* fix(sandbox): declare react framework deps and types so mfe-a typechecks\n\nmfe-a imports react/react-dom (React 19) but declared no deps, failing\nthe Sandbox typecheck step. Add the framework devDeps and point consumers\nto index.d.ts via the types field so mfe-b resolves the declared interface\ninstead of recompiling src/index.tsx under Solid JSX settings.\n\n* build: scope sync-versions postinstall to packages/* only\n\ntoolkit/* publishes independently (e.g. JSR) and keeps its own version.\nOnly the lockstep packages/* packages should be force-synced to root, so\nan intentional bump like syntax-highlighter 0.3.0 is no longer reverted\non every bun install.\n\n* build: link fe bin at workspace root so ''bun fe'' resolves in CI\n\nbun only links the @fe/cli fe bin into packages that declare it as a dep\n(devtools/store/network), not the repo root. The sandbox CI job runs\n''cd sandbox && bun fe check ...'', which walks to root node_modules/.bin\nand finds no fe, failing with ''Script not found fe''. Declaring @fe/cli as\na root devDependency makes bun link the bin into root node_modules/.bin.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"340927d40ebe2d2d2567e16cd0ef4beef0c4e382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/git/trees/340927d40ebe2d2d2567e16cd0ef4beef0c4e382"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/usually-frustrated/fe/git/commits/762d274858a95c844806fde382aed24e0e9a16ce","verification":{"payload":"tree 340927d40ebe2d2d2567e16cd0ef4beef0c4e382\nparent a77e8872ec0155054eeddf21a5de8785c8513a23\nauthor Sushruth Sastry <2114206+sushruth@users.noreply.github.com> 1788904166 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788904166 +0000\n\nfeat(syntax-highlighter): add CSS line numbers via data-linenumbers (#36)\n\n* feat(syntax-highlighter): add CSS line numbers via data-linenumbers\n\nLine count is computed as a by-product of the existing tokenizer pass\nin highlightPre (no second traversal). The count is written as the\ndata-linenumbers attribute value; CSS ::before { content: attr(...) }\nrenders the number column with zero new DOM nodes injected into code.\n\nBlocks with data-linenumbers scroll horizontally rather than wrap, so\nline numbers stay aligned against long lines.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* refactor(syntax-highlighter): restore applySheet as named function\n\nWas inlined unnecessarily to hit a hard line limit. The limit is a\nguideline; 181 lines is fine.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* docs: soften source file line limit to a guideline (σ≈5 around 180)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* fix(syntax-highlighter): enforce no-wrap invariant with !important\n\nwhite-space, overflow-x, and min-width are correctness constraints for\nline number alignment, not style preferences. !important prevents\naccidental CSS overrides from silently breaking number sync.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* feat(syntax-highlighter): release 0.3.0 with line numbers; update docs\n\n- Bump version 0.2.3 → 0.3.0\n- Add CHANGELOG.md\n- Add data-linenumbers to file/source code blocks in docs fragments\n  (architecture, platform-eng, product-eng, tutorials); shell commands\n  and short concept snippets left unchanged\n\nTo publish: cd toolkit/syntax-highlighter && bun run publish\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BEjyQ3NJxxQqBqQzdWqtKY\n\n* fix(sandbox): declare react framework deps and types so mfe-a typechecks\n\nmfe-a imports react/react-dom (React 19) but declared no deps, failing\nthe Sandbox typecheck step. Add the framework devDeps and point consumers\nto index.d.ts via the types field so mfe-b resolves the declared interface\ninstead of recompiling src/index.tsx under Solid JSX settings.\n\n* build: scope sync-versions postinstall to packages/* only\n\ntoolkit/* publishes independently (e.g. JSR) and keeps its own version.\nOnly the lockstep packages/* packages should be force-synced to root, so\nan intentional bump like syntax-highlighter 0.3.0 is no longer reverted\non every bun install.\n\n* build: link fe bin at workspace root so ''bun fe'' resolves in CI\n\nbun only links the @fe/cli fe bin into packages that declare it as a dep\n(devtools/store/network), not the repo root. The sandbox CI job runs\n''cd sandbox && bun fe check ...'', which walks to root node_modules/.bin\nand finds no fe, failing with ''Script not found fe''. Declaring @fe/cli as\na root devDependency makes bun link the bin into root node_modules/.bin.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoILmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsp0QADLLiT1CCDxtsH0HQpip/ILL\n1a5Y7Coww/QGOaYFm9nCfzbzyrBSxGDBaXWM0XbO8p+NQ1m77Zk5AMqQL6hGaqfl\n8plv4wpBMldHsw3zzGu+x7ch/Rluta8EFjO/HaTyikwGdUI5EbqQdxALFyznUJs8\nKjM+IFb5mXImMHLRymlrj7PVRtmJELUa/9HoBOqPUsuy6BQJL0tVMHBIhMWjh77b\nAH/Ed6f/VGxOuGEA0aKTPKY+iE5UeveLpQvwa71agyudY6PDrmqDWVMxAc91ToPM\nWawX6ylSUNZjICvEnc9EQyU+nUvFu0QGbYTDpdvF++QI4gEKDnQTmagXQ3ZAKB1R\n/HU3tXMhOLrvjNBEArr5hBhXsOwH1tjkHEePxDW2eecxg1mNO1BJI7KBoCig1FS/\n72eGdBS7HFSb2uPZvfh4hnas90dn9gaLFXHXCcA5fZUr7eWQCCsieBmTF1C9jOVN\nuDNkPoszkMraO/db21BKrHL/XrsBtlPOfvNKnZkcHiEm6Si5DSE85bvxd8aVVJu8\nKqtcKrmrp27Kpp+jv/XLR+tExrh7ohzw2wn2szGLFe0Ddh2znYwwshmaW18Cc8Oa\niUL2buH+1VXALx1DSEg78/7WLAvJ3+VIdSf/miXpt8v43C2sED3xG5TExKQHg3o/\nL7u5psg5dFSvCcWAzq09\n=zBk9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T21:49:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu