ptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sushruth","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sushruth/resume/commits/a15de00e9173e1887fdde3c07cca45cf0cfd58b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-03T21:39:13Z","email":"2114206+sushruth@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sushruth Sastry"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-03T21:39:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: migrate to Pause GitHub Action (#9)\n\n* Adding resume xmp data\n\n* Updates from Overleaf\n\n* Updates from Overleaf\n\n* chore: updated a tiny description to be more accurate\n\n* chore: cleanup\n\n* feat: add GitHub workflow for resume compilation and release\n\n* refactor(cli): improve consistency and robustness of LaTeX sync\n\n* docs: refine README to be more professional and clever\n\n* docs: improve READMEs for root and cli\n\n* chore: Tone down the principal stuff - Yes, I think I am ready but I\ndont want to be that desperate for that title. I dont particularly care.\n\n* chore: fixing file name and one minor issue with TAC team identity I\nhad.\n\n* chore: I dont know why I am still tweaking this. My imposter syndrome is\nstrong with this one.\n\n* chore: Yeah much better. too much fluff from AI before.\n\n* Attempting a fix on workflows\n\n* chore: fixing bun install issues in CI\n\n* ci: fixing alpine package names\n\n* chore: somehow claude always forgets permissions on workflows.\n\n* chore: refactor because why would I stop when it works? I stop when my\ndevs are happy - me.\n\n* refactor: type safety is king! so is documentation actually.\n\n* feat: cached docker build that expires only if Dockerfile changes + fond\nmemories for sererna mcp\n\n* chore: trigger warning - this is changing the triggers\n\n* feat: Improvements by a mentor, and a statement on adding AI related\nwork on my resume\n\n* refactor: migrate build system from Docker to Podman\n\n- Replace Docker with Podman in CI/CD workflow (release.yml)\n- Add --layers flag and cache-ttl for efficient layer caching\n- Use :Z volume mount suffix for SELinux compatibility\n- Create scripts/build.sh for local Podman-based builds\n- Simplify Dockerfile to use volume mounts instead of COPY commands\n- Configure GitHub Actions cache for Podman container storage\n\n* feat: better concurrency because I dont want to waste github action\ntime.\n\n* docs: update all documentation for Podman migration and add pre-commit review guideline\n\n- Update .github/workflows/README.md with Podman build strategy and concurrency control\n- Update .serena/memories/BUILD_AND_DEPLOYMENT.md with Podman commands and cache details\n- Add critical pre-commit documentation review guideline to AGENTS.md\n- Ensure all docs reflect current container runtime (Podman vs Docker)\n- Document new concurrency group behavior for automatic build cancellation\n\n* docs: add MCP tool usage and concise communication guidelines for agents\n\n- Require use of Serena MCP for code operations and ACP MCP for general file I/O\n- Prohibit long redundant summaries and ceremonial phrases\n- Enforce direct, actionable communication style\n\n* fix: replace texlive-full with minimal packages to avoid disk space issues\n\n- Use texlive base + luatex + latexextra + fontsextra\n- Covers all packages used: inputenc, tabularx, array, booktabs, microtype, hyphenat, colortbl, arydshln, pdfx, embedfile, geometry, xcolor, hyperref, enumitem, titlesec, standalone, import, babel\n- Reduces image size from ~5GB to <500MB\n\n* docs: update documentation for minimal TeX Live packages\n\n- Document minimal TeX Live package set in workflow and build docs\n- Note ~500MB vs ~5GB savings from texlive-full\n- List specific packages included in texmf-dist-latexextra\n- Add disk space troubleshooting guidance\n\n* Well, minor edit to docs\n\n* fix: add CJK language support to resolve CJKutf8.sty missing error\n\n- Add texmf-dist-langcjk package for CJK (Chinese/Japanese/Korean) support\n- Resolves LaTeX compilation error: File ''CJKutf8.sty'' not found\n\n* Use latex-action small scheme in CI\n\n* Update CI/CD pipeline to use GitHub CLI for releases, replacing deprecated actions and fixing asset path\n\n* feat: update infrastructure - switch Dockerfile to ubi9-minimal, add Bun/LaTeX caching, automate PDF naming with year, remove deleted scripts/Dockerfile refs from docs\n\n* fix: remove deprecated ''scheme'' and ''extra_packages'' inputs from latex-action, use pre_compile for package installation\n\n* fix: correct YAML indentation and variable expansion for YEAR in PDF name\n\n* Add HTML resume generation with LaTeX-like styling\n\n- Add HTML templates in cli/src/templates/ using EJS\n- Extend sync engine to generate resume/index.html\n- Update converters to use EJS for HTML rendering\n- Update documentation and gitignore for generated files\n- Add ejs dependency to CLI\n\n* Feat: html resume with cloudflare\n\n* chore: cleanup for HTML stuff\n\n* chore: html style update\n\n* chore: minor html tweaks\n\n* fix: cheap fix for bad mobile rendering on the html resume\n\n* chore: add aider files to gitignore\n\n* refactor: Update file paths and workflow triggers\n\n* docs: add deployment options guide and fix build.sh paths\n\n- Add comprehensive deployment guide for Cloudflare Pages, Vercel, Netlify, and Render.com\n- Fix build.sh to use absolute paths based on script location\n- Ensures build script works when called from any directory\n\n* docs: fix Cloudflare Pages configuration in deployment guide\n\n- Correct root directory path to ''infrastructure''\n- Update build command to ''bash build.sh'' (runs from root directory)\n- Clarify that build output directory is current directory\n\n* fix: use public directory for build output to avoid symlink issues\n\n- Create infrastructure/public directory for clean output\n- Avoids Cloudflare Pages symlink errors from node_modules\n- Update deployment docs with correct output directory\n- Add public directory to gitignore\n\n* docs: update all platform configurations to use public output directory\n\n- Update Vercel, Netlify, and Render.com configurations\n- Change output/publish directory from ''.'' to ''public'' for all platforms\n- Add troubleshooting section for symlink errors\n- Ensure consistent configuration across all deployment platforms\n\n* refactor: migrate to Pause GitHub Action\n\n- Delete infrastructure/ (Bun/TS CLI, LaTeX templates)\n- Delete docs/, .serena/\n- Add resume.json at root\n- Add Pause workflow\n- Update README and .gitignore\n\nBREAKING: Local build removed. Uses Pause GH Action now.\n\n* chore: remove migration plan\n\n* docs: update user-content and README for Pause architecture\n\n* refactor: symlink root README to user-content/README.md\n\n- Move README.md authority to user-content/README.md\n- Symlink root README.md to user-content/README.md\n- Update markdown links to be root-relative for portability\n\n* refactor: flatten file structure\n\n- Move contents of user-content/ to root\n- Remove user-content/ directory\n- Update Markdown links in README.md and AGENTS.md\n- Remove symlinks\n\n* ci: update pause action and fix schema validation\n\n- Update usually-frustrated/pause to pause-org/action@v1\\n- Add explicit YAML schema directive to fix editor validation errors\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Your Name <you@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"7042ed7739d9f4e3de02b8e0c18f60ff50ff8f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sushruth/resume/git/trees/7042ed7739d9f4e3de02b8e0c18f60ff50ff8f9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sushruth/resume/git/commits/a15de00e9173e1887fdde3c07cca45cf0cfd58b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7042ed7739d9f4e3de02b8e0c18f60ff50ff8f9a\nparent 3912c6b653e5b2dab251ce9e30052ae1f8930574\nauthor Sushruth Sastry <2114206+sushruth@users.noreply.github.com> 1770154753 -0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770154753 -0800\n\nrefactor: